  ('12cbcbb6-3106-493b-9caa-9c9e422176ad', 5,
   $q$He cast a Yea on SB 319 (2022 House Vote #817, 100-67; the same roll call is filed twice in the store and is counted once), whose operative text says 'no person shall carry a weapon unless he or she is a lawful weapons carrier' and defines a lawful weapons carrier as anyone 'licensed or eligible for a license', so the permit to carry is no longer required. That is rung 5: 'Repeal laws that require a permit or registration for a gun, such as the permit to carry'. He also cast a Yea on HB 1324 (2026 House Vote #665, 87-76), which strikes 'or silencer' from O.C.G.A. 16-11-122's dangerous-weapons ban, whose exception (16-11-124) is NFA registration, i.e. it takes an accessory off a registration law (annex R5-AZ), and he is a sponsor of HB 1324 (its floor vote was 87-76, so not gated). His Yeas on HB 218, HB 280, HB 292, HB 859, HB 1060 and SB 259 are rung 4 acts on the same side. His sponsorship of HB 1018 and HB 1454 (registry bans, merchant codes and discharge preemption) is direction-only or adjacent. HB 1023 is gated and SB 204 is multi-subject.$q$,
