  ('3ef10dd3-cdd7-4ab7-96c2-a08ab173a3e1', 5,
   $q$Rung 5 (repeal laws that require a permit or registration for a gun). He voted Yea on GA HB 1324 (2026-03-06, 87-76), single-subject, which strikes 'silencer' from the O.C.G.A. 16-11-122 dangerous-weapons ban whose only exception is possession 'registered' … 'in accordance with the dictates of the National Firearms Act' (R5-AZ: removing an accessory from a registration law). His other acts are a Yea on HB 1018 (a registry bar where none exists: R5-L direction-only), a gated Yea on HB 1023 (151-11) and a Yea on multi-subject SB 204; his 2022 line 'I will stand strong on supporting' … 'the Second Amendment' names no rule. No rung 1-3 act.$q$,
