  ('3f7bce23-9dbe-49a5-97b5-2ce4cb4a60c2', 5,
   $q$Rung 5 (repeal laws that require a permit or registration for a gun, such as the permit to carry). He voted Yea on GA SB 319 in the House (2022-03-30, 100-67), whose enacted text says 'no person shall carry a weapon unless he or she is a lawful weapons carrier' (anyone 'licensed or eligible for a license'), ending the carry-permit requirement, and in his own words (2023-01-31, quoted by a trade group) said of that bill 'Constitutional Carry. I was a co-sponsor, and proud to be that.' He also voted Yea on HB 1324 (2026-03-06, 87-76), which strikes 'silencer' from the O.C.G.A. 16-11-122 ban whose only exception is NFA registration (R5-AZ). His HB 1018 sponsorship (merchant codes adjacent; registry bar direction-only under R5-L) and his other loosening votes do not conflict; no rung 1-3 act.$q$,
