   $q$He voted Yea (2022-03-30, 100-67) on GA SB 319, which removes the permit to carry ('no person shall carry a weapon unless he or she is a lawful weapons carrier', meaning anyone 'licensed or eligible for a license'), and Yea (2026-03-06, 87-76) on HB 1324, which strikes 'silencer' from O.C.G.A. 16-11-122's ban whose exception is NFA registration (R5-AZ). Both meet 'Repeal laws that require a permit or registration for a gun, such as the permit to carry'. His other Yeas (HB 218, HB 280, HB 292, HB 859, HB 1060, SB 259) are rung 4 acts, HB 1018 is direction-only, HB 1023 is gated and SB 204 is multi-subject; no rung 1-3 act. SB 319 appears twice in the store; counted once.$q$,
