  ('79878ead-3065-4c47-8f42-711a39a72678', 5,
   $q$Rung 5, "Repeal laws that require a permit or registration for a gun, such as the permit to carry": prime sponsor of HB 1324 (its floor vote, 87-76, is not near-unanimous, so the sponsorship is not gated) and a Yea on HB 1324 (2025-26; House Vote #665, 2026-03-06, 87-76; single-subject, not gated), which strikes "silencer" from O.C.G.A. 16-11-122 ("No person shall have in his or her possession any sawed-off shotgun, sawed-off rifle, machine gun, or dangerous weapon" … "except as provided in Code Section 16-11-124"), a ban whose exception is items registered "in accordance with the dictates of the National Firearms Act": removing an accessory from a registration law (R5-AZ). His sponsorship of HB 1454 (2025-26) is a registry bar where none exists (direction-only, R5-L) plus a local-discharge preemption (adjacent). HB 1018 (2023-24) is a merchant-code rule (adjacent) plus a bar on a gun-owner registry where none exists (direction-only, R5-L); HB 1023 (weapon detection at school entrances, "weapon" wider than firearms) is a school-safety measure (adjacent) and is gated near-unanimous (151-11); SB 204 (2025) is multi-subject and its gun part is preemption (adjacent). No rung 1-3 act is on file.$q$,
